  "result": {
    "summary": "The exact frozen contextual bundle completed eight untouched 625-hand Slumbot sessions: 5000 hands at -51.75 bb/100, raw CI95 [-89.52,-13.98]. Stateful replay verified 15284 decisions and all context transitions; session independence passed. Cold-start512 scored +1.367 and active4488 -57.810 descriptively. Context changed only 228/13710 active decisions (1.663%). Against the execution-matched Standard10 bridge fresh20k (-24.5683), the independent delta was -27.1817 with CI95 [-69.1354,+14.7720].",
    "conclusion": "This frozen endpoint fails the directional external gate and must not be scaled to fresh20k/100k. The absolute external result is clearly negative, but it does not establish contextual mechanism collapse: action changes were sparse, changed-hand outcomes were not the loss source descriptively, and the execution-matched candidate-minus-base interval includes zero. Retain the method as underidentified/undertrained, reject this checkpoint for external promotion.",
    "decision": "REJECT_ENDPOINT512_EXTERNAL_PROMOTION_RETAIN_CONTEXT_METHOD_AS_UNDERIDENTIFIED",
    "next_step": "Run a no-new-Slumbot proxy/action-support alignment audit on the frozen 128/512 three-seed endpoints: replay broad training and SHA-disjoint holdout evaluations to measure contextual-vs-Standard10 argmax flip rate, margin, street/seat support, and whether paired gains concentrate on changed decisions. Use it to decide whether a margin-aware objective deserves a new multi-seed geometric training curve or whether to pivot to a different learned self-play objective."
  },
